From caa3e614bd8ff3017a9c716364dac7f9d6908f15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Dawid=20Wr=C3=B3bel?= <me@dawidwrobel.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 02:01:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/41] firmware: qcom: scm: add QSEECom app loading and
 listener services

The SCM layer already knows how to look up a loaded QSEE application and send
it a command. Two things are missing before a trusted application can be driven
from Linux.

Loading: qcom_scm_qseecom_app_load() hands TZ an MDT-described image and gets
back the application id. TZ needs the image at a physically contiguous,
suitably aligned address, and it keeps the name it was loaded under, which is
what a later app_get_id() matches on.

Listener services: a trusted application asks the normal world to do work on
its behalf -- file I/O above all -- by raising a listener request, and it stays
blocked until one is answered. Register a listener with its shared buffer,
service the requests TZ reports, and answer them with one of
enum qcom_scm_qseecom_listener_status. Unregistering guards against ids that
were never registered, which TZ reports as an error rather than ignoring.

Servicing subsumes qcom_scm_qseecom_check_result(): with incomplete calls now
answered rather than refused, the only case left for it is a call blocked on a
busy listener, reported where the servicing happens. The helper and its two
call sites go with it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
